{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the seven empty ears.</b> The reason he did not say the same concerning the seven years of plenty is that even in those days they were years of plenty, and there is nothing so novel — only that the plenty would increase, as he said (Genesis 41:29): ״שָׂבָע גָּדוֹל״ — the novelty being that the plenty would be great. Therefore he said only a wondrous new thing, which is years of famine." "<b>Further,</b> it appears that since the plenty is nothing but for the purpose of preparing for the years of famine, as he revealed at the end when he commanded to gather the produce of the years of plenty for the years of famine, therefore he mentioned only the years of famine, for that is the essence of the dream's being made known to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:29.443202610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}